.\" Template for dkim2-dsn-propagator(8). Edit this file, then run "make man".
.\" Lines starting with '.\" @cobra' are replaced by the real help text.
.TH DKIM2-DSN-PROPAGATOR 8 "2026-11-03" "dkim2" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
dkim2\-dsn\-propagator \- DKIM2 delivery\-status propagation adapter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" @cobra Usage dkim2-dsn-propagator
.SH DESCRIPTION
When a remote server bounces a message that this host forwarded under DKIM2,
the bounce must travel back to the previous hop.
.B dkim2\-dsn\-propagator
receives such a delivery\-status notification over LMTP, asks
.BR dkim2d (8)
to evaluate, rebuild, and sign the notification for the previous hop,
re\-injects it through a trusted local, Milter\-free SMTP listener, commits
the reserved propagation coordinate, and only then acknowledges the LMTP
transaction.
.PP
The adapter is transport glue: it never parses DKIM2 fields, rewrites a
message, chooses a recipient, or falls back to another signing route.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Create the configured LMTP Unix socket and serve until SIGTERM or SIGINT.
.TP
.B validate
Load the strict configuration and its propagation capability without opening
a socket or contacting the daemon.
It is silent on success.
.TP
.B probe
Reload the configuration and check that its socket is a single\-link Unix
socket owned by the effective UID with no permissions for other users.
It neither opens an LMTP session nor contacts the daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
.\" @cobra Flags dkim2-dsn-propagator
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every stable configuration path may also be supplied through its single
declared environment name: the path upper\-cased, with
.B .\&
replaced by
.BR _ ,
behind the
.B DKIM2_DSN_PROPAGATOR_
prefix.
A value set in both places is a configuration error.
Scalar values may contain
.B ${NAME}
placeholders, expanded before validation; a missing variable fails closed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, help output, or a clean shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, startup, validation, probe, or runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Command shape or flag error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/dkim2/propagation/lmtp.sock
LMTP socket used by the Postfix guide's
.B dsn_propagator
transport.
.TP
.I propagation capability
The 32\-byte capability for the daemon's two propagation operations (mode 0400
or 0600) in a parent of exact mode 0500.
No other route ever receives it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dkim2d (8),
.BR dkim2\-milter (8),
.BR dkim2ctl (1)
.PP
